  "prompt": "Is the family home deductible from the gross estate, and up to how much?",
  "runtimeCommit": "6ce2d6fd613e7f3109022f5a0f5ea006e9122546",
  "answer": "### Short Answer\nYes, the family home is deductible from the gross estate, up to a maximum amount of P10,000,000.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nIn practical terms, this means that when calculating the estate tax, the value of the family home can be excluded from the total value of the estate, up to the specified limit. This provision is particularly beneficial for families, as it helps ensure that a significant portion of the family residence is not subject to estate tax, allowing heirs to retain their home without the burden of a large tax liability.",
